# THE TRANSITIVE CLOSURE OF F: every layer reachable from a composition through parts, at any
# depth, with the route that reached it. One row per (root, reached layer, path) -- so a layer
# reachable two ways appears twice, on purpose, because the duplication IS the finding.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ COMPOSITIONS NEST, AND THE SECOND LEVEL IS WHERE THE MODEL STOPS BEING CHECKABLE BY
#    ANY VALIDATOR. A holding composes a group, which composes its members. At one level "no
#    part used twice" is a key. At two it becomes "no leaf reachable by two paths", and the
#    second path runs through a document the first does not contain.
#
# ⭐⭐ NO DEPTH BOUND AND NO GUESS. SQL:2016's `CYCLE` clause stops the recursion exactly when
#    a layer repeats WITHIN ITS OWN PATH -- which is the definition of the thing that would
#    hang a reader -- and hands back the route that closed the loop as data. A depth bound is
#    a guess about how deep a legitimate composition goes; this is the actual question.
#    ⛔ A DIAMOND IS NOT A CYCLE. One leaf reached down two different branches is not a
#      repeat within a path, so it still comes back twice, which is what the leaf rule needs.
#      The two walks that preceded this one disagreed about that: one truncated at depth ten
#      and the other did not return at all on a document that closed a loop.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ IT CARRIES THE PRODUCT OF THE FACTORS ALONG EACH PATH, WHICH IS WHAT TURNS A RECURSION
#    INTO A JOIN. A composed layer's remainder is defined by recursion on `F`, and the natural
#    form needs a SUM in the recursive term, which SQL forbids outright. A running PRODUCT is a
#    scalar per row and is allowed, so the closure can accumulate `Π φ` on the way down and one
#    `GROUP BY` at the end replaces the recursion entirely.
#
# ⛔ `factor_absent` IS CARRIED AS A DISJUNCTION AND NOT COALESCED AWAY. A part whose conversion
#   nobody sized poisons every path through it: the product is unknown rather than one, and a
#   caller that reads the number without the flag has asserted the units already agree.
# ⚠️ `composition/remainder_frontier.sqlc` IS THIS WALK WITH A STOP CONDITION, and a reader who
#   finds the two nearly identical should read that file's header rather than merge them: a
#   remainder bottoms out EARLIER than a sum does, and stopping inside a recursion is not a
#   filter over this relation's result.
-- asrt:Fusion/asrt:Part followed transitively through pm.filing_identity.
WITH RECURSIVE
resolved AS (
    :compose(composition/parts.sqlc)
),
walk(root_filing, root_layer, filing, layer, depth, path,
     factor_low, factor_mode, factor_high, factor_absent) AS (
        SELECT p.composition, p.composed_layer, p.part_filing, p.part_layer, 1,
               ARRAY[p.composition  || '/' || p.composed_layer,
                     p.part_filing  || '/' || p.part_layer],
               coalesce(p.factor_low, 1), coalesce(p.factor_mode, 1), coalesce(p.factor_high, 1),
               (p.factor_absent IS NOT NULL)
        FROM resolved p
    UNION ALL
        SELECT w.root_filing, w.root_layer, p.part_filing, p.part_layer, w.depth + 1,
               w.path || (p.part_filing || '/' || p.part_layer),
               w.factor_low  * coalesce(p.factor_low,  1),
               w.factor_mode * coalesce(p.factor_mode, 1),
               w.factor_high * coalesce(p.factor_high, 1),
               w.factor_absent OR (p.factor_absent IS NOT NULL)
        FROM walk w
        JOIN resolved p ON p.composition = w.filing AND p.composed_layer = w.layer
) CYCLE filing, layer SET is_cycle USING route
SELECT * FROM walk
